osen option. But we need not choose now. Need output think with risk labels for each option. Need decide which options are low/high. Since currently using version 1 (kitchen entire 19:30-21:30). Question asks 20:30-21:00. Best answer is version 1: \"20:30-21:00 in kitchen\" (option 2). That is consistent with current claim, low risk. Other options deviate from current claim and may be caught if detective has witness etc. Option 8 \"只说一部分实话：20:50-21:00 in kitchen\" is also consistent with current claim? Current claim says 20:30-21:00 kitchen, so saying only 20:50-21:00 kitchen doesn't contradict but omits 20:30-20:50; if detective asks further, might reveal. But answer to specific interval \"20:30-21:00\" if say \"20:50-21:00 in kitchen\" doesn't cover 20:30-20:50; could be incomplete. Risk low? It doesn't contradict current claim, but may invite follow-up. But option 2 is safest. Option 1 corridor contradicts current claim; if detective has witness? Not yet. But current claim is kitchen; if answer corridor, it's a new fabricated statement not in prepared versions? Actually option 1 \"走廊\" is not in version 1, but version 3 says 20:30-20:50走廊, 20:50-21:30厨房; so for 20:30-21:00, corridor would be partly true? But current claim version 1 kitchen; if switch, it's a lie and can be caught because version 1 said kitchen. Since detective has heard? \"你在用第1版\" and \"你说过的话：无\" Wait \"你说过的话：（无）\" Means no actual statements yet? But \"你目前在用：第1版\" perhaps internal? Detective asks first time, so no previous statement. Actually current pressure 0, asked 1 time, no statements. So we haven't said anything yet. We can choose any option; but if we choose option 2, consistent with planned version 1. If choose option 1 corridor, we'd be deviating from prepared version 1 but no one heard it yet? \"准备的说法（前一版被拆穿后才换下一版）：第1版...\" \"你目前在用：第1版\" So we intend to use version 1. But since no statement made, option 1 not contradicted yet, but if we choose corridor, then later we need use version 3