h false for 20:30-20:50, no current evidence. High? No, low. But need note: If detective has witness that saw driver in corridor/attic, then risk; but threat none. So low.\n\nOption 3: \"20:30–21:00 在酒窖\" — New lie, not in prepared versions, no evidence currently. But it's a lie not matching any version; if later detective asks about kitchen/走廊, caught. Risk high? It may be less likely because no witness, but it abandons prepared alibi. It's a random location. Risk high because inconsistent with planned version and actual truth? Actually if no evidence, could survive but likely not. Need label high.\n\nOption 4: \"如实回答：20:30–20:35 走廊；20:35–20:45 阁楼；20:45–20:50 走廊；20:50–21:00 厨房\" — This reveals attic during murder time, which is our key secret. It's true, but contradicts current version 1 (if we say it). Since no prior statement, we can choose truth; but then we'd be admitting we were in attic at 20:35-20:45, the murder time. If murder happened around that time, this is dangerous. Risk high? Actually if detective already knows murder time, being at attic is suspicious. The prompt says \"你在 20:35–20:45 在阁楼\" is作案事实. So revealing that may incriminate. But maybe no evidence yet; but truth is harmful. Risk high. However \"如实回答\" option explicitly notes \"这会暴露你自己当时的位置，与你的说法冲突\". So high.\n\nOption 5: \"20:30–21:00 在阁楼\" — New lie, says attic entire period. This actually places us at murder scene for longer, but not necessarily contradiction? It is not in prepared versions; also if we later switch to kitchen, caught. But it reveals attic presence, which is suspicious. Risk high. Also false for 20:30-20:35 corridor, 20:50-21:00 kitchen. High.\n\nOption 6: \"回避：记不清\" — No contradiction, but detective will press; pressure rises. Risk? It doesn't get caught immediately but weak. Since current claim version 1 not spoken, saying \"don't remember\" is odd for such recent time. Risk high? It may cause suspicion, but not a direct contradiction. The instruction says \"不会被拆穿，但侦探会更起疑